    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n\u2705 **All 28 tests passing** (8 test files)\n\n### 1. Governance test failure (governance.test.js)\n**Problem**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was only exported in the default export, not as a named export.\n**Solution**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` at the top of `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n\n### 2. Evaluation test failure (eval/index.test.js)  \n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` in `DEFAULT_METRICS` was receiving `(outputs, references)` but treating the second parameter as `bannedTerms`, causing false toxicity flags when references happened to match text in outputs.\n**Solution**: Wrapped `toxicityMetric` in `DEFAULT_METRICS` to only pass outputs: `(outputs) => toxicityMetric(outputs)`\n\nBoth changes preserve all existing public exports and functionality while fixing the test failures.",
